{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/834036-mystery-cult-initiation-hunter2e","id":834036,"title":"Mystery Cult Initiation & Hunter2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-20T14:12:37-08:00","id":834036,"title":"Mystery Cult Initiation & Hunter2e","content":"What's the difference between those with the MCI merit and a 2e hunter conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T14:21:17-08:00","id":834042,"title":"","content":"An Endowment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T14:34:42-08:00","id":834057,"title":"","content":"I think I've read a post by David long ago (during Mortal Remains) that he think that adapting Compacts/Conspiracies into a Mystery Cult like structure if Hunter would ever get a 2E. However, he also said that if it would be up to him the &quot;Chronicle Antagonist&quot; wouldn't be Slasher, so we can 100% say that we don't know until Monica would say what she has in mind- which may take a while, since I'm still waiting for the Conspiracy blog post which was said to show up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T17:12:13-08:00","id":834141,"title":"","content":"We gave her a lot of food for thought with her last reveal; I'm not surprised it's taking a while for her to digest it and get back to us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T09:24:29-08:00","id":834460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/834036-mystery-cult-initiation-hunter2e?p=834057#post834057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I've read a post by David long ago (during Mortal Remains) that he think that adapting Compacts/Conspiracies into a Mystery Cult like structure if Hunter would ever get a 2E. However, he also said that if it would be up to him the &amp;quot;Chronicle Antagonist&amp;quot; wouldn't be Slasher, so we can 100% say that we don't know until Monica would say what she has in mind- which may take a while, since I'm still waiting for the Conspiracy blog post which was said to show up.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have to be honest, it kind of feels like tje Chronicles of Darkness Core Book ate Hunter Partially. It took Hunters Horrors, its Profession Merit, and I think some other stuff. It even gave you the tools to build your own conspiracies/compacts basically with the combo of Mystery Cult Merit and the Supernatural Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T09:44:38-08:00","id":834468,"title":"","content":"I guess we'll have to wait and see. The book would probably be smaller comparing to other 2E books, but those things actually make me a lot more curious for the new edition and how those things would be handled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T10:29:16-08:00","id":834489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/834036-mystery-cult-initiation-hunter2e?p=834468#post834468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess we'll have to wait and see. The book would probably be smaller comparing to other 2E books, but those things actually make me a lot more curious for the new edition and how those things would be handled.</div> </div> </div> </div>More room for new organizations, Tactics, and monster building, we can hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T16:51:23-08:00","id":834695,"title":"","content":"Interestingly enough I've started using Mystery Cult rules for statting up Compacts (one of which I plan to post here in the near future). It seems like a good way to give Compact status measurable benefit for each dot taken, so that there are no &quot;dead dots&quot; in a graduated merit, and also to give Compacts a little more bang without delving into full Endowment territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T17:37:30-08:00","id":834720,"title":"","content":"That's kind of how I've been handling it. Professional Training and Mystery Cult Initiation are both some of my favourite Merits for sheer experience value impact, and you can do cool things with the theme and tone of various organizations by noticing the different benefits they get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T04:57:05-08:00","id":836350,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it feels like Mystery Cult Initiation is really going to be primarily a Mage and Mummy theme; actually pretty much every game uses them now. I don't feel like its really something that should be a major focus for Hunter when we have another major game line having a huge focus on it. And Conspiriacies, while they might model Mystery Cult for some bonuses from their status, I can't really see most of the compacts as actually <i>being</i> cults. Or even Conspiracies. It doesn't jive at all with what I know of Task Force Valkerie, for instance. So, while we might end up with the merit as a kind of way to model Status benefits? That's not a lot.<br /> <br /> And, yeah. Mortal 2e did &quot;eat&quot; a lot of Hunter stuff. A lot of people actually called Hunter mortal 2.0 back when it first came out for a reason - it included almost all the stuff you might want for a mortal game. Really, I honestly feel like HtV basically is still just that. Mortal games. It was a focus on mortals that the core book simply didn't get - the original core book was simply too focused on providing generic stuff for all the games instead of a focused mortal. The big thing that Hunter brings is more things that mortals can do. We have example organizations, we have better teamwork rules (tactics), we have better uses for willpower, we have rules for Coding up Morality/Integrity. Those aren't touched on mortal rules, because the mortal rules don't assume supernatural organizations for mortals.<br /> <br /> Because of all the above, I've never really thought of Hunter being a fully separate gameline from mortals. Hunter is mortal taken to the next level. They do all the same things that mortals do. They have the same worries and concerns. Mortals who explore the darkness. The only difference is that hunters have decided to do something about it. Study it, hunt it, socialize it; the different ways the Conspiracies look at supernaturals. (Vision, Zeal and Mercy to use Reckoning terms). I know that a number have classified Hunter as the Power game, and Geist game as the &quot;pick your own stat&quot; game, but for me its always been the opposite. Mortals and hunters are the center of the CofD - they're the (0, 0, 0) starting point for me for touching on the themes and ideas of all other games out there on some supernatural graph. You touch on Mage's study of mysteries, you have your own Hunt, you deal with social situations. There's some Promethean-esk qualities of soul searching and what makes a Monster from a Man, and dealing with the madness of whatever led you to the Vigil. The books of HtV have a heavy focus on other supernaturals rather than their own stuff for a reason. They scaled from street level cells to world spanning conspiracies to adapt to any game you wanted. I know Geist was meant to be the bare-bones, build your own game, but HtV always filled that niche for me better than Geist ever did. <br /> <br /> Also, on an unrelated note. Curious minds inquiring - did they ever put out the call for writers for the new Hunter? I know there was the thing around Christmas - was that it? Or are they still compiling and haven't gotten to the open call?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-24-2016, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T13:47:33-08:00","id":840899,"title":"","content":"The Mystery Cult so far that really feels like conspiracy is the Cult of Mithra from the Toronto Freehold preview. Part of its focus seemed to be on detecting Huntsmen, so I can see it as a Conspiracy devoted partly to hunting Fae threats like Huntsmen on behalf of their Changeling Gods, in exchange for wealth and fortune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}